<section class="concept-section" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">UNDERSTAND THE BUILDING BLOCKS</p>
      <h2>From model response to <span class="accent-text">coordinated work.</span></h2>
      <p>These capabilities work together. An organization can combine only the pieces its use case needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="concept-flow">
      <article class="concept-step reveal"><span class="concept-symbol">M</span><span class="concept-kind">MODEL</span><h3>Generate</h3><p>A language model interprets an input and generates an output.</p></article>
      <span class="concept-connector" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      <article class="concept-step reveal"><span class="concept-symbol">R</span><span class="concept-kind">RAG</span><h3>Ground</h3><p>Retrieval adds relevant information from selected knowledge sources.</p></article>
      <span class="concept-connector" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      <article class="concept-step reveal"><span class="concept-symbol">A</span><span class="concept-kind">AGENT</span><h3>Act</h3><p>An agent can choose tools and take steps toward an assigned task.</p></article>
      <span class="concept-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article class="concept-step concept-step-outcome reveal"><span class="concept-symbol">↗</span><span class="concept-kind">WORKFLOW</span><h3>Coordinate</h3><p>Orchestration connects people, agents, tools, and systems around a business process.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="concept-caption">The right architecture depends on the task, the available data, and the level of autonomy the organization chooses.</p>
  </div>
</section>

